# Device patch paths, one per line in application order.
#
# One core patch is named by neither the ARM64 nor the OS series, and the official
# records say it must still be present: docs/xnu/patch-reference.md lists
# sheng-platform-power under the platform series, and
# docs/.vitepress/device-records/sirius.toml records for sdm710 that "the ARM64 and
# OS series assume the two files they omit are present". The board layer supplies
# it here through the same arch: prefix the OS series uses for
# zzz-boot-progress.patch; nothing here is a device-local rewrite of XNU.
#
# native-smp-secondary and native-smp-type-clusters used to be carried here the
# same way, because UniXNU-sm8250-common@6bb9b025 shipped an empty
# patches/xnu/series. The feed is now pinned at a6e7e36 (the pin the official
# SM8250 board alioth uses), whose SoC series applies both, so they are gone from
# this file: the SoC owns them, and the two are only valid as a pair - the
# cluster-type tags in dts/dby_w09.dts need native-smp-type-clusters.patch, which
# is what raises MAX_CPU_CLUSTERS to 2 and defines __ARM_AMP__.
# scripts/check-smp-topology.py is the gate that refuses the unpaired form.
#
# sheng-platform-power: the sheng_pmgr_run() call site in bsd_init.c that
# CONFIG_XNU_SHENG_PMGR=y needs, and the block zzz-boot-progress.patch quotes as
# unchanged context at its @@ -773,7 +775,9 @@ hunk.
#
# Order in [kernel] patch_series: this file is still listed before os: rather than
# last. git apply runs the resolved sequence literally (scripts/unixnu/patches.py
# prepare), and the OS series' zzz-boot-progress.patch hunk only applies once the
# block above already exists, so the canonical arch/soc/os/device order cannot be
# satisfied while sheng-platform-power has no series of its own.
arch:../../../patches/xnu/sheng-platform-power.patch
